hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16712","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, that a man who served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eight years narrated to him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when his food was brought near him, say: In the name of Allah, and when he finished his food say: O Allah, You fed and gave drink and enriched and sufficed and guided and gave life, so praise be to You for what You gave."
